Demonstration Flow

Step 1: Open the ComicCraft application.

Step 2: Introduce the project:

ComicCraft – AI Comic Story Creator using Gemini Models

Step 3: Explain the problem of manually creating comic stories.

Step 4: Explain the proposed AI-based solution.

Step 5: Enter a sample story idea.

For example:

“A shy student discovers a tiny robot that can repair broken things.”

Step 6: Select a genre such as Science Fiction.

Step 7: Enter characters such as Maya and Robo.

Step 8: Select the number of panels.

Step 9: Select the target audience.

Step 10: Click Generate Comic.

Step 11: Show the generated:

* Title
* Genre
* Logline
* Characters

Step 12: Scroll through the generated panels and explain:

* Scene
* Narration
* Dialogue
* Characters

Step 13: Show the ending and moral.

Step 14: Demonstrate Download Comic JSON.

Step 15: Demonstrate Download Comic HTML.

Simple Viva Explanation

“Our project is ComicCraft, an AI Comic Story Creator using Gemini Models. The main purpose of this project is to convert a simple story idea into a structured comic storyboard. The user provides the story idea, genre, characters, number of panels and target audience. These details are sent to the Gemini AI model through a structured prompt. Gemini generates the title, characters, scenes, narration and dialogues. The generated response is validated using Pydantic and displayed through a Streamlit interface. Finally, users can download the generated comic in JSON or HTML format.”

